{"type":"npc","name":"Neoctri","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":75,"temp":0,"max":75,"details":""},"ac":{"value":21,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["aklo","chronan","common"],"details":""},"level":{"value":5},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Neoctri spend much of their time seeking out powerful organisms to consume and new environments to prompt valuable adaptations. Whenever possible, they choose intelligent prey and engage in prolonged hunts, only killing their victims when they are confident those victims have no more tricks in store. Though neoctris are merciless, they can be convinced to spare their targets at least temporarily in exchange for sufficiently enticing information about ways to enhance their abilities. Neoctris recognize that their forms don't allow them to walk freely in settlements, and they don't hesitate to take hostages and engage in other tactics of terror to coerce people into helping them get the information they seek.</p><p>When neoctris meet each other, the outcome is typically bloody and vicious, with both combatants seeking to learn from each other's adaptations. Neoctris have no compunctions about killing each other, but their sense of self-preservation often means that when one gets the upper hand, the other prioritizes escape.</p><p>Combating a neoctri requires constant alertness. They can undergo rapid evolution in mere seconds, modifying their defenses, enhancing their attacks, and creating new modes of locomotion, so it's especially foolish to become complacent after observing a neoctri's initial assault. Cultures who encounter a rare neoctri often pass down fables with the following moral: it's never wise to underestimate a neoctri.</p><h2>Hunting the Hunters</h2><p>One of a neoctri's favorite tactics is to isolate and hunt a single member of a humanoid community. The neoctri follows their victim, foiling their every stratagem, until the victim is near defeat—only to let them escape at the last moment. When the terrified humanoid raises the alarm and the community's defenders venture forth to catch the neoctri, the hunters become the neoctri's new prey, to be picked off one by one.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 18/45/80 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing, slashing), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Intimidation, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, charisma, constitution, energy resistant (acid, cold, electricity, fire, sonic, vitality), music, sensory (darkvision, scent), spiked, strength, time, wild</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 18/45/80 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing, slashing), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Intimidation, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, charisma, constitution, energy resistant (acid, cold, electricity, fire, sonic, vitality), music, sensory (darkvision, scent), spiked, strength, time, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Ron Branchaud","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":11,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"scent","acuity":"imprecise","range":30}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":12,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":11},"athletics":{"base":13},"intimidation":{"base":13},"survi